    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0670" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg574"/>

                <head>No. 348.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 13, 1874</date>.
                        (Received Nov. 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 17th of
                    January last, transmitting copies of the Treasury Regulations governing the
                    transportation of dutiable merchandise between the Dominion of Canada and the
                    United States, I have already had the honor to inform you that I had forwarded
                    those documents to the Governor-General of Canada.</p>
                <p>I have now the honor to inclose copies of a dispatch and of its inclosures, which
                    I have received from his excellency in reply to my communication on the above
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDW’D THORNTON.</signed></closer>





